INT. NEON ARENA - ESPORTS TOURNAMENT - NIGHT

Rain on the glass roof of the arena. Thousand of fans in the dark with glowing sticks, the casters voices loud on the speakers, blue light on every face, and under the stage Wei in a fake staff jacket is carrying a cable box past two security guards who are watching the big screen and not him while Jonas sits at the final table with his headset on, his hand perfectly steady on the mouse and Bianca stands in the back corridor with a coffee she is not drinking.

Smoke machine. Bass in the floor. Somewhere a child crying from happiness.

WEI
(he wipes his palms on the jacket)
Box is in. Two minutes.

JONAS
(headset on, eyes on the screen, he clicks twice)
You said one minute before.

WEI
(he checks the watch)
The guard changed. It happens.

BIANCA
(she puts the coffee down on a crate)
Then we are not late. We are just on time slower.

JONAS
(a tiny nod, he does not look at either of them)
Bianca your voice is too loud.

The rain gets harder. A bright flash from the stage, the crowd screams, the casters say a name that is not Jonas.

BIANCA
(she moves closer to the door)
They are looking at you. The man in the grey suit. Left side.

WEI
(he puts the box down very slowly)
Which man.

BIANCA
(she does not point, she only lifts her chin)
The one who is not clapping.

Wind pushes at the roof. Cold air comes under the door. Far away a guard laughs at something on his phone.

JONAS
(he types something fast, then removes his hands from the keyboard and puts them on his knees)
Done. Money is moving. Nobody stand up.

WEI
(he smiles with only half of his mouth)
Then why is your leg shaking.

JONAS
(he presses the knee flat with his palm)
Because I am going to win this game also.

BIANCA
(she opens the door a little, one finger on the handle)
The grey suit is gone.

Nobody speaks. On the screen the countdown goes to ten.
